nale":"Felbatol is the FDA/US trade name; Taloxa is a non-US/EMA trade name for felbamate. The deterministic suggestion to add 'Felbamate' as a trade name should not be applied because felbamate is the generic/product ingredient name, not a distinct trade name.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=33488","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/taloxa"]},{"current_value":"","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"","rationale":"Important brand aliases are already captured in trade_names; no additional generic PubMed alias is required.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8347179/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1944909/"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA labeling and FDA orphan approval records support US approval/availability for Felbatol/felbamate.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%222f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=33488"]},{"current_value":"1993","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"1993","rationale":"FDA orphan approval page lists Felbatol/felbamate marketing approval date as 07/29/1993. The prior deterministic concern that 1993 was not label-concordant is not a contradiction; approval year is verified by FDA approval records rather than the current label text.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=33488"]},{"current_value":"Focal; LGS; Generalized","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Focal; LGS; Generalized","rationale":"FDA labeling supports use in adults for partial seizures with and without generalization, and in children for partial and generalized seizures associated with Lennox-Gastaut syndrome.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=33488"]},{"current_value":"Tablet; oral suspension","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Tablet; oral suspension","rationale":"FDA labeling lists 400 mg and 600 mg tablets and 600 mg/5 mL oral suspension.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Adults: 1200-3600 mg/day divided TID/QID","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Adults: 1200-3600 mg/day divided TID/QID","rationale":"FDA dosing instructions initiate adult therapy at 1200 mg/day divided three or four times daily and titrate to 2400-3600 mg/day when indicated.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"1200 mg/day","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"1200 mg/day (recommended adult initial dose; not independently established as a minimum effective dose)","rationale":"The FDA label supports 1200 mg/day as the recommended adult starting dose. It does not establish this as a formal minimum effective dose.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"3600 mg/day","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"3600 mg/day","rationale":"FDA labeling describes adult titration to 3600 mg/day and pediatric LGS maximum of 45 mg/kg/day or 3600 mg/day.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8347179/"]},{"current_value":"14-23 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"20-23 h","rationale":"FDA labeling states a terminal half-life of 20-23 hours in subjects with normal renal function. The label separately notes renal impairment prolongs half-life by 9-15 hours, but does not support 14-23 h as the normal range.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver","rationale":"NCBI/StatPearls describes hepatic metabolism via CYP enzymes; FDA labeling also describes metabolites/conjugates after oral administration. Note that FDA labeling also reports substantial unchanged urinary excretion, so this field should not be read as primary elimination route.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/n/statpearls/article-21669/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Inhibits CYP2C19; induces CYP3A4","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Inhibits CYP2C19; weakly induces CYP3A4","rationale":"Trusted FDA/NCBI-accessible evidence supports CYP2C19 inhibition and interaction evidence consistent with weak CYP3A4 induction, including reduced gestodene exposure. Adding 'weakly' better matches the literature and interaction magnitude.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6009244/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2016/205836Orig1s000_205837Orig1s000_205838Orig1s000ClinPharmR.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Anticonvulsant mechanism is unknown in labeling; proposed mechanisms include reduced seizure spread with NMDA receptor inhibition and GABA-A receptor modulation.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Anticonvulsant mechanism is unknown in labeling; proposed mechanisms include reduced seizure spread, antagonism at the glycine site of the NMDA receptor-ionophore complex, and GABA-A receptor modulation.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports unknown clinical mechanism, reduced seizure spread in animal models, weak GABA-receptor binding effects, and NMDA glycine-site antagonism. The proposed wording is more precise than generic 'NMDA receptor inhibition'.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32165193/"]},{"current_value":"Moderate","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Moderate","rationale":"The mechanism is not established in labeling, but there is FDA label and peer-reviewed mechanistic support for GABA/glutamate-related effects. Moderate confidence is reasonable.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32165193/"]},{"current_value":"FDA label","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA label; peer-reviewed review","rationale":"The FDA label supports the 'unknown mechanism' and preclinical NMDA/GABA statements; the Sills and Rogawski review supports broader ASM mechanism classification. Current tier omits the peer-reviewed component used by the cell.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32165193/"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No QT/QTc warning or clinically meaningful QT effect identified in reviewed FDA labeling","rationale":"The FDA label describes no clinically significant mean blood-pressure or heart-rate changes, but it does not provide a dedicated QT/QTc study statement. The current value is plausible but stronger than the located source support.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"insufficient_evidence","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"GI: anorexia 19%, GI: vomiting 17%, CNS: insomnia 16%, GI: nausea 12%, CNS: headache 12%, hematologic/hepatic: aplastic anemia/hepatic failure <1%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"Adult controlled add-on trials: CNS: headache 36.8%, somnolence 19.3%, dizziness 18.4%, insomnia 17.5%; GI: nausea 34.2%, anorexia 19.3%, vomiting 16.7%, dyspepsia 12.3%; hematologic/hepatic: aplastic anemia and hepatic failure are boxed-warning risks and incidence is not reliably quantified in labeling.","rationale":"The current row mixes or rounds unsupported percentages. FDA adult add-on controlled-trial table gives headache 36.8%, nausea 34.2%, anorexia 19.3%, vomiting 16.7%, insomnia 17.5%. The boxed warning states aplastic anemia/hepatic failure risks are serious and not reliably quantified, so '<1%' is not source-supported.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Restricted-use ASM for severe/refractory epilepsy because of serious aplastic anemia and hepatic failure risks.","field":"status_or_notes","proposed_value":"Restricted-use ASM for severe/refractory epilepsy because of serious aplastic anemia and hepatic failure risks.","rationale":"FDA labeling and NCBI LiverTox support restricted use because of aplastic anemia and acute liver failure risks.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548256/"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Wikipedia anticonvulsant drug-class list; FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labeling; NCBI LiverTox felbamate; FDA orphan drug approval record; PubMed RCT records; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review; EMA Taloxa EPAR for non-US trade name","rationale":"Wikipedia is not a trusted source for this audit, and DailyMed is not permissible for FDA boxed-warning verification. The proposed source list uses trusted domains and matches the row facts more directly.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%222f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548256/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=33488","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32165193/","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/taloxa"]}],"generic_name":"felbamate","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo RR50 differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo RR50 differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included PubMed placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"The included PubMed RCT abstracts/records do not provide an arm-specific drug-minus-placebo 50% responder-rate differential. Cochrane add-on review notes only one non-row included study reported 50% responder outcome, and placebo-randomized RR50 data were not reported there.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10210023/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7796796/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8347179/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8469324/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2044501/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1944909/","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9342851/"]},{"current_value":"23 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: FelbamateStudyGroupinLennoxGastautSyndrome1993 felbamate up to 45 mg/kg/day or 3600 mg/day 23%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"23 percentage points (felbamate 19% decrease in total seizure frequency vs placebo 4% increase; FelbamateStudyGroupinLennoxGastautSyndrome1993, felbamate up to 45 mg/kg/day or 3600 mg/day; not confirmed as a median percent change in the PubMed abstract)","rationale":"PMID 8347179 verifies the 23 percentage-point differential from 19% decrease versus 4% increase in total seizure frequency. However, the cited PubMed abstract does not describe this as a median percent change, so the current MPC wording overstates the metric specificity.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8347179/","https://www.fda.gov/media/158280/download"]},{"current_value":"FelbamateStudyGroupinLennoxGastautSyndrome1993|23|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8347179/|73","field":"plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"FelbamateStudyGroupinLennoxGastautSyndrome1993|23|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8347179/|73","rationale":"The numeric differential 23 and sample size 73 are supported by PMID 8347179. The same caveat applies: the metric is a total seizure-frequency percent-change differential, not clearly a median percent-change differential in the abstract.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8347179/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included PubMed placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"The included PubMed RCT records do not provide an extractable seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen. Presurgical trials report time-to-fourth-seizure or fourth-seizure event proportions, not seizure freedom.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7796796/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8469324/","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9342851/"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=2f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66; published=Dec 31, 2025; title=FELBATOL (FELBAMATE) TABLET FELBATOL (FELBAMATE) SUSPENSION [VIATRIS SPECIALTY LLC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=2f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=2f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66; effective_time=20250815; title=Felbatol / FELBAMATE; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%222f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for FDA boxed-warning verification in this audit; use FDA/openFDA metadata instead.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%222f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"14-23 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"20-23 h","reason":"FDA labeling supports terminal half-life 20-23 hours in normal renal function; 14-23 h was not verified against FDA label text.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"GI: anorexia 19%, GI: vomiting 17%, CNS: insomnia 16%, GI: nausea 12%, CNS: headache 12%, hematologic/hepatic: aplastic anemia/hepatic failure <1%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"Adult controlled add-on trials: CNS: headache 36.8%, somnolence 19.3%, dizziness 18.4%, insomnia 17.5%; GI: nausea 34.2%, anorexia 19.3%, vomiting 16.7%, dyspepsia 12.3%; hematologic/hepatic: aplastic anemia and hepatic failure are boxed-warning risks and incidence is not reliably quantified in labeling.","reason":"Current percentages conflict with FDA adverse-event tables and '<1%' for aplastic anemia/hepatic failure is not supported by labeling.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"23 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: FelbamateStudyGroupinLennoxGastautSyndrome1993 felbamate up to 45 mg/kg/day or 3600 mg/day 23%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"23 percentage points (felbamate 19% decrease in total seizure frequency vs placebo 4% increase; FelbamateStudyGroupinLennoxGastautSyndrome1993, felbamate up to 45 mg/kg/day or 3600 mg/day; not confirmed as a median percent change in the PubMed abstract)","reason":"23 is verified, but the cited abstract supports a total seizure-frequency percent-change differential, not explicitly a median percent-change differential.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8347179/"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Wikipedia anticonvulsant drug-class list; FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labeling; NCBI LiverTox felbamate; FDA orphan drug approval record; PubMed RCT records; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review; EMA Taloxa EPAR for non-US trade name","reason":"Use trusted audit sources and remove Wikipedia/DailyMed dependency.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%222f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548256/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=33488","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32165193/","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/taloxa"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA or FDA/accessdata labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","reason":"DailyMed should not be relied on where FDA/openFDA or FDA label sources are available; mechanism claims are supported by FDA labeling and peer-reviewed review.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32165193/"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No QT/QTc warning or clinically meaningful QT effect identified in reviewed FDA labeling","reason":"The row's stronger negative QT claim is not directly established in located FDA labeling; the proposed text is limited to reviewed source evidence.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Siegel1999","pmid":"10210023","proposed_action":"Retain; optionally note that PubMed does not explicitly label the phase.","rationale":"PMID, drug, and design are concordant: felbamate add-on to valproic acid in Lennox-Gastaut syndrome; abstract describes FBM or placebo titration for two 7-week observation periods with washout, and PubMed types include randomized controlled trial/controlled clinical trial. Phase II/III label is not explicit in PubMed metadata.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10210023/"},{"label":"Devinsky1995","pmid":"7796796","proposed_action":"Retain; optionally note that PubMed does not explicitly label the phase.","rationale":"PMID, drug, and design are concordant: felbamate monotherapy in refractory partial seizures; abstract states double-blind randomized placebo-controlled trial with titration to 3600 mg/day vs placebo. Phase II/III label is not explicit in PubMed metadata.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7796796/"},{"label":"FelbamateStudyGroupinLennoxGastautSyndrome1993","pmid":"8347179","proposed_action":"Retain; optionally note that PubMed does not explicitly label the phase.","rationale":"PMID, drug, and design are concordant: 73 patients with LGS received add-on felbamate or placebo for 70 days, titrated to 45 mg/kg/day or 3600 mg/day; PubMed types include randomized controlled trial. Phase II/III label is not explicit in PubMed metadata.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8347179/"},{"label":"Bourgeois1993","pmid":"8469324","proposed_action":"Retain; optionally note that PubMed does not explicitly label the phase.","rationale":"PMID, drug, and design are concordant: double-blind placebo-controlled felbamate trial in 64 presurgical partial-onset seizure patients; efficacy variable was time to fourth seizure. Phase II/III label is not explicit in PubMed metadata.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8469324/"},{"label":"Theodore1991","pmid":"2044501","proposed_action":"Retain; optionally note that PubMed does not explicitly label the phase.","rationale":"PMID, drug, and design are concordant: randomized double-blind three-period crossover felbamate study in complex partial seizures; PubMed record includes placebo as a substance and the abstract compares placebo and felbamate periods. Phase II/III label is not explicit in PubMed metadata.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2044501/"},{"label":"Leppik1991","pmid":"1944909","proposed_action":"Retain; optionally note that PubMed does not explicitly label the phase.","rationale":"PMID, drug, and design are concordant: double-blind randomized placebo-controlled clinical trial of felbamate for partial seizures; abstract reports felbamate vs placebo seizure-frequency outcomes. Phase II/III label is not explicit in PubMed metadata.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1944909/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=2f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66; published=Dec 31, 2025; title=FELBATOL (FELBAMATE) TABLET FELBATOL (FELBAMATE) SUSPENSION [VIATRIS SPECIALTY LLC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=2f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=2f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66; effective_time=20250815; title=Felbatol / FELBAMATE; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%222f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5","reason":"DailyMed source is not permitted for boxed-warning verification by the audit instructions.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%222f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Wikipedia anticonvulsant drug-class list; FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labeling; NCBI LiverTox felbamate; FDA orphan drug approval record; PubMed RCT records; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review; EMA Taloxa EPAR for non-US trade name","reason":"Current source list includes Wikipedia and DailyMed; trusted row support should use FDA/openFDA/accessdata, NCBI/PubMed, and EMA sources.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%222f522701-397a-11de-8a39-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548256/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=33488","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32165193/","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/taloxa"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA or FDA/accessdata labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","reason":"Replace DailyMed naming with FDA/openFDA or accessdata FDA labeling while retaining the peer-reviewed review source.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/020189s027lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32165193/"]}],"summary":"Felbamate row is mostly concordant for identity, availability, indications, formulations, dosing, trade names, FDA approval year, mechanism, and RCT links. Updates are needed for policy-compliant FDA boxed-warning source metadata, evidence source list, adverse-event percentages, half-life, and wording of the 23% outcome as a percent-change differential rather than confirmed median percent change."}
